Feature: Login Functionality\n\n  Scenario: User navigates to the login page\n    Given the user navigates to \"https://practicetestautomation.com/practice-test-login/\"\n    Then the login page should display a username field, a password field, and a login button\n\n  Scenario: User logs in with valid credentials\n    Given the user is on the login page\n    When the user enters \"student\" in the username field\n    And the user enters \"Password123\" in the password field\n    And the user clicks the login button\n    Then the user should be redirected to the dashboard\n    And the dashboard should display the message \"Congratulations! You logged into a secure area!\"\n\n  Scenario: User logs in with invalid username\n    Given the user is on the login page\n    When the user enters \"invalidUser\" in the username field\n    And the user enters \"Password123\" in the password field\n    And the user clicks the login button\n    Then an error message \"Your username is invalid!\" should be displayed\n    And the user should remain on the login page\n\n  Scenario: User logs in with invalid password\n    Given the user is on the login page\n    When the user enters \"student\" in the username field\n    And the user enters \"wrongPassword\" in the password field\n    And the user clicks the login button\n    Then an error message \"Your password is invalid!\" should be displayed\n    And the user should remain on the login page\n\n  Scenario: User leaves username and password fields empty\n    Given the user is on the login page\n    When the user leaves the username field empty\n    And the user leaves the password field empty\n    And the user clicks the login button\n    Then a message \"Username and password cannot be empty.\" should be displayed\n\n  Scenario: User enters username exceeding input limit\n    Given the user is on the login page\n    When the user enters a username with more than 50 characters\n    And the user enters \"Password123\" in the password field\n    And the user clicks the login button\n    Then an error message should be displayed indicating input limit exceeded\n\n  Scenario: User enters password exceeding input limit\n    Given the user is on the login page\n    When the user enters \"student\" in the username field\n    And the user enters a password with more than 50 characters\n    And the user clicks the login button\n    Then an error message should be displayed indicating input limit exceeded\n\n  Scenario: Login button is disabled until both fields are populated\n    Given the user is on the login page\n    When the user enters \"student\" in the username field\n    And the user leaves the password field empty\n    Then the login button should be disabled\n    When the user enters \"Password123\" in the password field\n    Then the login button should be enabled\n